        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d7778594-d0c4-5867-b66e-b247b40269bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ernest Whitington\n- Places: South Australia, London\n- Organizations: The Register, The Advertiser, South Australian Register\n- Roles: Journalist, Columnist\n- Works: \"Out among the People\"\n- Events: Newspaper amalgamation, South Australian Register publication and closure\n\nFacts:\n- The South Australian Register was first published in London in June 1836.\n- The South Australian Register ceased publication in February 1931, almost a century after it began.\n- Ernest Whitington was born around 1873 and died on 13 April 1934.\n- Ernest Whitington was a journalist in South Australia and was known to his friends as \"Ern.\"\n- Ernest Whitington wrote the popular \"Out among the People\" column under the pen name \"Rufus\" in The Register.\n- After The Register and The Advertiser were amalgamated, Ernest Whitington continued writing \"Out among the People\" in The Advertiser.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
